# Code owners are requested for review automatically on every pull request.
#
# Combined with the branch ruleset option "Require review from Code Owners",
# this is what makes an approval from anyone else insufficient to merge: an
# outside contributor may leave an approving review, but it does not satisfy
# the requirement, so the merge button stays disabled until an owner approves.
#
# To add another approver, append their username to these lines, e.g.
#   *    @Ahd-Aljadeed @some-trusted-admin
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners

# Default owner for everything in the repository.
*       @Ahd-Aljadeed

# Build, CI and deployment configuration — changes here decide what gets
# published and what is allowed to skip the checks.
/.github/           @Ahd-Aljadeed
/vite.config.js     @Ahd-Aljadeed
/playwright.config.js @Ahd-Aljadeed
/package.json       @Ahd-Aljadeed
/package-lock.json  @Ahd-Aljadeed

# Security-relevant helpers: escaping and untrusted-input validation.
/src/utils/sanitize.js  @Ahd-Aljadeed
/src/utils/validate.js  @Ahd-Aljadeed

# The test suites themselves — weakening a test is how a regression sneaks in.
/test/  @Ahd-Aljadeed
/e2e/   @Ahd-Aljadeed
